Structure: two-compartment (WSS one-compartment 13.870 [Hessian PD TRUE], two-compartment 1.596 [Hessian PD TRUE]; two-compartment adopted only if WSS drops by > 5.99); see pk_structure_summary.csv and pk_structure_comparison.csv
C24 (24 h after the acute dose): observed NTX 2.1, BN 17.6 ng/mL; one-compartment predicts NTX 2.95, BN 21.87; two-compartment predicts NTX 2.10, BN 21.72. At least one structure reproduces both 24 h values within a factor of 1.5.
Objective statistics: C24, Cmax, thalf, Tmax; CV floor 0.10 (Tmax 0.25)
Final WSS 1.5960; Hessian eigenvalues (of hessian/2): 155.2, 116, 35.39, 18.57, 13.28, 4.085, 0.4757; positive definite: TRUE
ka 1.860 per h (absorption half-life 22.4 min)
Observations 12 (8 single-dose, 4 once-daily at steady state; regimen column of pk_summary.csv) and 12 nominally distinct (regimen, analyte, stat) combinations, but only 11 distinct predicted values to 6 significant figures and 10 to 3 (the single-dose and steady-state terminal half-lives are the same quantity in a linear model: NTX coincides exactly, BN to 0.1%). With 7 fitted parameters: nominal residual degrees of freedom 5, EFFECTIVE 4 (3 at 3 significant figures).
Tmax check: NTX observed 1.00 h, predicted 1.00 h; BN observed 2.00 h, predicted 1.96 h
Parent naltrexone disposition half-lives: distribution 1.23 h, terminal 9.79 h; smallest Hessian eigenvalue 0.476 (largest 155)
Fixed parameters: fp fixed at 0.95: the approved naltrexone labelling gives oral bioavailability of 5 to 40 per cent, i.e. a systemic parent fraction (1 - fp) of roughly 0.05 to 0.40; 0.95 sits at the UPPER EDGE of that range (1 - fp = 0.05) and inside the region where the weighted SSE is flat (change <= 0.29 for fp 0.9 to 0.999 in the free fit). Occupancy sensitivity at fp = 0.90 and 0.99 is reported (pk_fit_sens_fp090.rds, pk_fit_sens_fp099.rds) and is immaterial (occupancy moves by at most 0.001).
Limitation (stated; no structure added): the chronic (once-daily, steady-state) 6-beta-naltrexol Cmax is under-predicted, 103.7 vs observed 158.4 ng/mL (0.65-fold). With the 24 h concentrations in the fit, linear kinetics cannot also produce the observed 1.8-fold rise of the chronic over the acute peak; Verebey 1976 itself reports no trough accumulation. The observation's CV (0.57) keeps its weight low.
Unbound fraction of 6-beta-naltrexol: fu_BN = 0.79 is taken EQUAL TO THE PARENT's fu_NTX by fallback: no 6-beta-naltrexol plasma-protein-binding value was found (data/README.md 'Not found' list). It is an assumption, not a measurement, and it scales every unbound 6-beta-naltrexol concentration.
